course: dictionary
lesson: 2460
title: A French word in English
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some English words come from other languages, and ballet has many of them. «Danseuse» is a French word. In French it simply means dancer, a woman who dances.
explain: In English, a danseuse is almost always a female ballet dancer. «Première danseuse» means a leading female dancer, the star of the company. You will mostly meet this word in old-fashioned or formal writing, because today most people say ballerina or dancer.
explain: Context shows you the pattern. «Job words change in patterns: boulanger to boulangère, chanteur to chanteuse, acteur to actrice; so danseur gives danseuse.» The ending changes to show that a woman is doing the job.
fact: Danseuse is a noun, so you can say a danseuse, or danseuses for more than one.
fact: «Danseuse» means a female ballet dancer.
fact: «Première danseuse» means a leading female dancer.
fact: In French, «danseuse» simply means dancer, a woman who dances.
fact: Today English speakers usually say ballerina or dancer instead of danseuse.
exercise: «The première danseuse took a bow at the end of the performance.» What does danseuse mean? | *A female ballet dancer | A kind of ballet shoe | A male ballet dancer | A theatre seat
exercise: Dani says danseuse is just a fancy word for dancer. What is the best answer? | A type of French cake | A stage with lights | A male dancer at a disco | *A female ballet dancer, used mostly in ballet and formal writing
exercise: Which word means a leading female dancer? | Boulangère | Danseur | Chanteuse | *Première danseuse
test: Following «job words change in patterns», what does danseur become for a woman dancer? | Dansant | *Danseuse | Danseurs | Danseusse
test: What does the French word «danseuse» mean on its own? | A singer | A cook | A bridge | *A dancer, a woman who dances
exam: Which word is a female dancer in ballet? | acteur | fermière | danseur | *danseuse
